      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think the best solution would be to put the avatar parameters on a new line below all the other columns, instead of cramped in the left column. Make the Parameter name sub-column the width of the longest parameter name, to a maximum of the full width minus the width of the Type and Value sub-colums.\n\nAn alternative simpler solution would be to just display the ends of the parameter names, and truncate off the beginning of the names instead. The end of a parameter name tends to be the most useful, especially since even without these new contact parameters, people are encouraged to use long parameter names separated by slashes for organizational reasons.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-10-21T19:00:40.631Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The new Advanced Contact Parameters are almost all cutoff when viewed in the debug window due to their long names. This makes debugging them kind of annoying. For example, in the included screenshot at a glance I have no idea which of the collision tag parameters is which unless I remember the order I assigned them on the contact itself.\n\nLong parameter names already had this issue and I'm not sure what a solution to this problem would be, just wanted to raise awareness of this as it has been slightly annoying.",
